WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.880
What if just one
lifestyle change

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.680
could help you
avoid getting cancer,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.520
or diabetes,
or heart disease,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.960
or high blood pressure?

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.240
This one change could cut
your risk of chronic disease

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.080
and add years to your life.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.840
Well, the simple solution to
so many of these problems

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.160
is to eat a healthy diet.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.520
In other words, one centered
around whole plant foods.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.120
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.240
I'm your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.240
There are lots of things you can do
to reduce your risk of getting cancer.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.880
Avoid tobacco,
maintain a healthy weight.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:44.320
But one of the simplest kinds of cancer
prevention is to follow a healthy diet.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.840
“The vast majority of cancer research
is devoted to finding cures,

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.320
rather than finding new ways
to prevent disease.”

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.760
And the results of these skewed
priorities are plain to see:

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.000
2021 is the 50th anniversary of
Nixon’s declaration of war on cancer,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.880
and the death tolls from the
most common forms of cancer

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.920
in the United States
have continued unabated.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.040
“We have been looking at the very
nature of cancer in the wrong way.”

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.560
Breast cancer doesn’t begin
when a lump is first detected.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.560
All the common cancers like lung,
colorectal, breast, and prostate

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.640
(which account for the majority of deaths)

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.000
have a long latency period—
often 20 years or more.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.960
So, it’s not like you were healthy,
and then one day you got cancer.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.040
You haven’t been healthy—you’ve had
cancer growing in you for decades.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.360
Indeed, there’s a bizarre
misperception that people are ‘healthy’

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.400
until they have actual
symptoms of invasive cancer.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.600
But “[t]he barn in which hay is smoldering

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.960
before it bursts into flames
is not a safe place.”

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.440
What about using diet and nutrition
to prevent and treat cancer?

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.000
Okay, but what kind of cancer?
There are more than 200 types of cancer.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.880
Ah, but they all share the same hallmarks.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.760
In a series of papers cited
more than 40,000 times

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:08.320
in the biomedical literature, ten hallmarks
of cancer have been identified.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.400
Increased sensitivity to growth factors;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.560
evading your body’s tumor suppressors;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.000
dodging your immune system;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.360
being able to grow forever;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.200
tumor promoting inflammation;

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.960
the ability to invade and spread
and hook up its own blood supply;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.800
the accumulation of DNA mutations;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.360
disarming the self-destruct
mechanisms in place;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.680
and hijacking the cell’s metabolism.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.560
And yes, of course, there are classes
of drugs to try to counter each one—

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.720
chemotherapy agents designed to target
each piece of the cancer puzzle.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.880
Now ideally, there would be drugs
able to target multiple hallmarks

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.160
at the same time, but that’s
not how drugs tend to work.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.000
And this is one of the major reasons why,
in the context of cancer research,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.880
there are so many proponents of
investigating plant foods,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.440
as they can deliver a cocktail of bioactive
compounds—bioactive compounds

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.400
that may target most, if not all,
of the hallmarks of cancer.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.200
Here’s a sampling of compounds
found in fruits and vegetables

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.440
such as berries, greens, and broccoli,
shown to be able to target

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.840
each of the ten hallmarks of cancer,
at least in a petri dish.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.480
Moreover, they ﬁt the characteristics
of an ideal chemopreventive agent.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.680
If you were to design the perfect
candidate, you’d want them to be

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.000
selective for cancerous or
precancerous cells

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.120
while leaving normal cells alone,
be side effect free,

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.160
target most types of cancers,
be able to be consumed as a part

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.880
of a daily diet, be conveniently
available almost everywhere,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.000
and be relatively inexpensive to boot.
And plants have all of these.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.520
So no wonder those eating more plant-based
tend to have lower cancer rates.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.920
However, it should be understood
that we’re not talking about

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.760
taking supplements containing extracts
or puriﬁed phytochemicals,

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.320
but rather eating whole
plant foods themselves;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.560
more of a food-system based approach
to targeting the hallmarks of cancer.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.360
Foods contain many thousands of
substances that lead to vast numbers

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.800
of possible interactions, yet
much of nutritional science

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.920
has long been directed towards the
impact of single dietary components.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.360
Yes, this kind of ‘reductionist’
approach can reveal

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.040
the role of individual nutrients or
foods in the development of disease,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.400
but let’s think about what the
optimal research strategy would be

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.360
to study the effects of bioactive
natural plant compounds

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.320
on disease prevention.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.880
Instead of using isolated phytochemicals
in the management of cancer,

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.080
how about using whole foods, because
sometimes the whole can be

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.920
greater than the sum of its parts,
a concept known as food synergy.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:34.080
Check out this study. The simultaneous
inhibition of a series

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.880
of cancer stages in breast cancer cells
using a phytochemical super-cocktail.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.080
Two breast cancer cell lines
were treated with six different

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.360
plant compounds individually,
and then all together,

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.560
at the level you might find in
your bloodstream after eating foods

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.520
like broccoli, grapes, soybeans, and turmeric.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.200
And while the compounds
were ineffective individually,

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.560
in combination they significantly
suppressed breast cancer

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.480
cell proliferation by
more than 80 percent,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.600
inhibited cancer cell
migration and invasion,

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.520
stopped the cancer cells in their tracks,

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.280
and eventually killed them all off.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.600
The plant compounds did all this
without having any deleterious effects

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.800
on the normal noncancerous
cells used as control.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.760
No wonder the foundation of cancer
prevention, based on an update

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.720
of the most extensive report on
diet and cancer ever published

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.800
is not pills, but plants.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.800
Cut down on alcohol, soda,
meat, and processed junk,

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.360
and center your diet around whole grains,
vegetables, fruits, and beans.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.360
In our next story, we look
at whether choosing organic

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.080
over conventional fruits and vegetables
could protect against cancer.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:46.080
In a review updating the evidence
on human exposure and toxicity

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.680
of pesticides, the body of evidence
linking pesticide exposure

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.360
and cancer is said to be so
huge that the role of pesticides

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.000
in cancer development
can no longer be doubted.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.080
But most of the evidence that shows
DNA damage from pesticides is from

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.080
occupational exposure among
farmers and workers in the fields,

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.760
the pesticide industry itself, or
those living in high spray areas.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.760
There is evidence linking
non-occupational exposure

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.880
to pesticides to DNA damage —
in this case single- and

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.080
double-stranded DNA
fragmentation in sperm of men —

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.280
with higher levels of pesticides
flowing through their bodies —

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.040
but that was in China, where the
average pesticide concentrations

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.080
are as much as four times higher
than in some other parts of the world.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.320
Another way pesticides could
potentially facilitate tumor growth

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.200
is through adverse effects
on anticancer immunity.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.960
NK cells, natural killer cells,
are our body's first line

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.360
of white blood cell defense against
cancer cells and virus-infected cells.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.080
And pesticides have been shown
to induce harmful effects

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.600
on these defender cells, reducing
their ability to kill off tumor cells.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.600
For example, if you put a bunch
of natural killer cells in a petri dish

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.840
along with human leukemia cells
without any pesticide, your natural

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.160
killer cells can clean house and wipe
out more than half of the cancer.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.440
But if you drip a tiny bit of pesticide
on, your NK cells are so disabled

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.200
that the cancer wins the day.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.480
Okay, but how much
pesticide are we talking?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:16.160
The researchers used the
maximum level found in those

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.840
actively spraying pesticides.
Most of us, however,

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:22.880
are privileged enough not
to be forced into such a job.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.720
So what about looking at just
the residual pesticides left

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.320
on conventional produce?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.400
Is choosing organic for cancer
prevention worth the investment?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:36.800
In the United States, more than 90%
of the population has detectable

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:41.040
pesticides in their urine and blood,
regardless of where they work or live.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.400
And we know it's from the food
we eat because crossover trials —

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.640
where people are switched between
consuming conventionally grown

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:50.480
and organic foods — show you can
turn on and off urinary concentrations

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.200
of pesticide metabolites
like a light switch.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.840
But that doesn't necessarily mean
the pesticides are harming you.

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:59.200
The health consequences
of consuming pesticide residues

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.920
from conventionally grown
foods remain unknown.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:05.440
But a recent study did find
that those who self-reported

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.240
the highest frequency
of organic food consumption

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:12.160
had about a 25% lower
risk of getting cancer.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:15.600
And here it is: the first of its kind
to evaluate the association

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.600
between frequency of organic food
consumption and cancer risk,

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.240
controlling for a wide
array of other factors.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.960
Doesn't it matter that organic
consumers are younger?

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:27.280
The researchers controlled
for that and still found

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.120
significantly lower cancer risk.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.840
Okay, but maybe organic consumers
get less cancer because

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.480
they're more affluent, or
more highly educated,

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.400
or skinnier or exercise more,

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:40.480
or eat less meat, or smoke less.
Nope, they controlled for all that

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:44.480
and still found significantly lower
cancer risk in organic consumers.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:48.000
Maybe their diets were different
in other ways though:

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.640
more fruits and vegetables
overall or less junk food?

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:54.560
Nope, they still found
significantly lower cancer risk.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:58.240
They concluded: our results indicate
that higher organic food consumption

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.560
is indeed associated with a reduction
in the risk of overall cancer.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:08.000
This is the most sophisticated study
of its type to date, but there was

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.840
an earlier study that was even bigger,
and little evidence was found

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.240
for a decrease in the
incidence of all cancers

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.040
except for perhaps one kind of
blood cancer, non-Hodgkin lymphoma.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.320
Here are the data.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.360
No difference in cancer overall
between those who never choose

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:27.520
organic or those who usually or always
do, with the only significant findings:

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:32.880
a lower risk of non-Hodgkin lymphoma
and an increased risk of breast cancer.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:36.880
Is it possible that women who choose
organic food are more conscientious

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.800
about getting screened
for breast cancer and that

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.920
explains the higher diagnosis rate?
We really don't know.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.880
Of course, what we care about
the most is not just cancer

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.120
but so-called all-cause mortality,
the risk of dying prematurely, period,

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:53.440
and higher blood levels of a pesticide
known as beta-hexachlorocyclohexane

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.480
are associated with living
a significantly shorter life.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.280
How do we cut down on our levels?

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.640
Well, there was a study done way back
when that found that the breast milk

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:07.600
of a vegetarian mother was found to
have less beta-hexachlorocyclohexane

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:11.360
than the milk of her sister, who
was also breast-feeding at the time,

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.520
but included meat in her diet.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:16.000
The vegetarian sister apparently
had levels of that pesticide

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.840
that were lower by about a third,
compared with her omnivorous sibling.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.120
No surprise, since this class of
chlorinated pesticides are fat soluble,

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:28.080
so they're found most frequently
in foods of animal origin.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:32.720
A more recent study failed to look
at beta-hexachlorocyclohexane,

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:37.040
but they did find that chlorinated
PCBs were associated

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.400
with increased mortality risk.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.440
And again, the toxins were found
in the same kinds of foods:

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.320
dairy products, eggs,
and animal fats.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.920
So, no surprise, the blood of those
eating vegan was found to be

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:51.040
significantly less polluted
than omnivores

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.560
regarding a whole series
of PCBs, including those found

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:57.120
in the study to be associated
with increased mortality,

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.760
but the vegans did not have lower
levels of beta-hexachlorocyclohexane.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.600
The bottom line is that if you're
worried about the adverse

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.960
health effects of pesticides
and pesticide-type compounds,

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.840
you may want to lower
your intake of animal products.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.240
But when it comes to fruits
and vegetables, the benefits

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:17.040
of consuming conventionally
grown produce are likely

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.720
to outweigh any possible risks
from pesticide exposure.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.480
So concerns over pesticide risks
should not discourage us

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:28.960
from stuffing our faces with as many
fruits and vegetables as possible.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:31.360
That would give us
a huge health benefit,

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.000
whereas the potential lifelong
damage of any pesticides

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.640
on those same fruits and
veggies has been estimated

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:40.560
to only cut a few minutes
off a person's life, on average,

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.680
which is nothing compared
to the nutritional benefits

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.167
of eating more fruits and vegetables.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.000
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.200
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:57.040
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.280
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:06.480
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
